---
description: "skill-builder — build or audit any AI agent skill from a description when user invokes /skill-builder"
alwaysApply: false
---

When user says `/skill-builder`, follow `skills/skill-builder/SKILL.md`.

**Invocation**: `/skill-builder "description" [--type workflow|mode|tool|reference|agent] [--repo] [--audit path] [--fix]`

**Phases (create path)**:
1. Route: detect --audit flag; if present jump to Phase A
2. Classify skill type (auto-detect or --type flag)
3. Gather requirements (≤3 questions total)
4. Domain research: WebSearch official docs for each tool/API the skill references (skip if no references needed)
5. Generate SKILL.md (frontmatter + body for type)
6. Generate references/ (verified facts only — no guessing)
7. Generate hooks/ (mode skills only)
8. Scaffold full repo (--repo flag only)
9. Report + install commands

**Phase A (--audit path)**:
1. Read SKILL.md at given path
2. Run full quality checklist from `references/skill-anatomy.md`
3. Output audit report: failures / warnings / passed count
4. If --fix: output corrected SKILL.md (fix failures only, don't rewrite passing sections)

**Critical**:
- `name` must match `^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*$`, max 64 chars
- `description` max 1024 chars; SKILL.md body max 5000 tokens
- Claude Code extended fields: `argument-hint`, `when_to_use`, `model`, `effort`, `context`, `agent`, `paths`
- Never output raw `{TEMPLATE_VARIABLES}` in generated files
- Domain facts in references must come from WebSearch of official docs — never guessed
- Reference files >100 lines need TOC at top; one-level-deep only (no chained includes)
- Load `references/skill-types.md` at Phase 0; `references/agent-rules.md` at Phase 7 only
